    <node id="NCMEC">
      <data key="d0">NCMEC</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">NCMEC is a private, nonprofit organization that plays a vital role in the clearinghouse for reports of child sexual exploitation, tasked with forwarding these reports to law enforcement agencies.&lt;SEP&gt;The National Center for Missing &amp; Exploited Children (NCMEC) acts as a clearinghouse for reports related to child sexual abuse material and may forward such reports to federal law enforcement.&lt;SEP&gt;The National Center for Missing &amp; Exploited Children (NCMEC) is responsible for receiving reports of child sexual abuse content as mandated by law.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bddbca1d37abd901742b0ca6610124c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03af3b99beed5a891fbf02b542aed03e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecd054a4b792109f9e8db4282abab32f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1756577150</data>
    </node>
    <node id="18 U.S.C. §2258A">
      <data key="d0">18 U.S.C. §2258A</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">18 U.S.C. §2258A is a US legislation imposing mandatory reporting obligations for child sexual abuse content.&lt;SEP&gt;18 U.S.C. §2258A is a section of U.S. law that mandates the forwarding of reports of apparent child pornography and related information to NCMEC.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03af3b99beed5a891fbf02b542aed03e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bddbca1d37abd901742b0ca6610124c1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1756577151</data>
    </node>
